,"    order=['Violation', 'No Violation', 'Others']\n",")\n","plt.title('Distribution of Article 8 Conclusion Outcomes (2010-2023)', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Conclusion Outcome', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Cases', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1aM0Pmh-_cjV"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","Category \"Others\" covers all cases where the `type` in Conclusion column is not mentioning either violation or no-violation.\n","Several possibility of cases under this category are:\n","- Inadmissibile cases : The text mentions \"Article 8\" because the applicant tried to sue under it, but the Court never reached the \"Facts\" or \"Law\" stage to decide if a violation occurred.\n","- Procedural Absorption (of another article) :  The text might say, \"In view of the finding under Article 6, the Court considers it unnecessary to examine the complaint under Article 8. Since the Court declined to rule, there is no \"Violation\" or \"No Violation\" label assigned.\n","\n","Therefore, during further analysis below and for model training later, we have decided to exclude cases from the \"Others\" category and focus only on \"Violation\" and \"No Violation\" cases."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"hqZxYhLOp01A"},"source":["####4.1.1 Case Outcome per year\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"ELuWK40Mp5tt","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":416},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790641924,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":471,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"abc71f8a-ec4d-4811-f423-f5c1bf86161e"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Calculate outcomes per year\n","outcomes_per_year = df_art8.groupby(['year', 'outcome_category']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n","\n","# Sort by year to ensure correct plotting order\n","outcomes_per_year = outcomes_per_year.sort_index()\n","\n","# Exclude 'Others' category\n","outcomes_per_year = outcomes_per_year.drop(columns=['Others'], errors='ignore')\n","\n","# Reorder columns to ensure consistent color mapping\n","expected_columns = ['Violation', 'No Violation']\n","current_columns = outcomes_per_year.columns.tolist()\n","ordered_columns = [col for col in expected_columns if col in current_columns]\n","ordered_columns.extend([col for col in current_columns if col not in expected_columns])\n","outcomes_per_year = outcomes_per_year[ordered_columns]\n","\n","# Plotting the stacked bar chart\n","plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n","ax = outcomes_per_year.plot(\n","    kind='bar',\n","    stacked=True,\n","    color=[PALETTE.get(col, '#cccccc') for col in outcomes_per_year.columns],\n","    ax=plt.gca()\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Article 8 Conclusion Outcomes Per Year (2010-2023) - Excluding Others', fontsize=18)\n","plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Cases', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.yticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='Outcome Category', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"KnpZIEWh3MnQ"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","Case volume spiked sharply in 2021-2022 — the two highest years in the dataset, likely reflecting a combination of post-pandemic processing of a backlog and the surge of pending Russian cases being resolved following Russia's expulsion from the Council of Europe in March 2022 after its invasion of Ukraine. Cases against Russia, which had historically been one of the largest sources of Article 8 violations, were processed and concluded before the Court's jurisdiction over Russia formally lapsed. The ratio of Violation to No Violation rema