()\n","\n","# Filter df_art8 for only these top 10 countries\n","df_top_countries = df_art8[df_art8['country_name'].isin(top_10_countries)].copy()\n","\n","# Group by year and country_name to count cases\n","cases_per_year_per_country = df_top_countries.groupby(['year', 'country_name']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n","\n","# Sort by year for plotting\n","cases_per_year_per_country = cases_per_year_per_country.sort_index()\n","\n","# Reorder columns to match top 10 order\n","cases_per_year_per_country = cases_per_year_per_country[top_10_countries]\n","\n","# Create a mapping from country names (from cases_per_year_per_country.columns) to their ISO codes\n","# This assumes 'country_names' dictionary is globally available from a previous cell, which it is.\n","name_to_iso_code = {name: iso for iso, name in country_names.items()}\n","# Create a palette that maps country names to colors from COUNTRY_PALETTE\n","line_plot_palette = {name: COUNTRY_PALETTE.get(name_to_iso_code.get(name), '#cccccc') for name in cases_per_year_per_country.columns}\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(16, 9))\n","sns.lineplot(data=cases_per_year_per_country, dashes=False, marker='o', palette=line_plot_palette)\n","\n","plt.title('Number of Article 8 Cases Per Year for Top 10 Respondent Countries (2010-2023)', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Cases', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='Respondent Country', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"usb6VWlHj4wd"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","The 2022 spike is almost entirely attributable to Russia (blue), whose cases surged to their highest point in the dataset before dropping sharply in 2023 as the Court concluded pending proceedings following Russia's expulsion from the Council of Europe in March 2022. This pattern appears to be the effect of geopolitical context rather than a genuine trend in Article 8 litigation.\n","\n","Also notable is Ukraine's steady increase in cases (orange), which rises from 2021 and becomes the leading respondent country by 2023 as Russian cases recede. This is consistent with the ongoing conflict generating new human rights complaints against Ukraine, and reflects the Court's continued jurisdiction over Ukraine, unlike Russia, meaning Ukrainian cases will persist in future datasets."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"DQePuk2Luiko"},"source":["###4.3 Article Pairing"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"tT3BFBh5tflS","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":686},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790642401,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":61,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"103b437b-893b-4ad8-bf5e-7e761452f081"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Distribution of Article 8 Citation Types:\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["                       count\n","article_citation_type       \n","Mixed Articles           894\n","Article 8 Only           427"],"text/html":["\n","  <div id=\"df-5ae73b16-4da1-4101-9595-f2bc1fa84065\" class=\"colab-df-container\">\n","    <div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>count</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>article_citation_type</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Mixed Articles</th>\n","      <td>894</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Article