with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["def categorize_article_citations(article_list):\n","    \"\"\"Categorizes if a case cites only Article 8 or Article 8 with other articles.\"\"\"\n","    if not isinstance(article_list, list) or not article_list:\n","        return 'No Article Info'\n","\n","    article_list_cleaned = [str(a).strip() for a in article_list]\n","\n","    if '8' in article_list_cleaned:\n","        if len(article_list_cleaned) == 1:\n","            return 'Article 8 Only'\n","        else:\n","            return 'Mixed Articles'\n","    else:\n","        return 'Not Article 8 Case'\n","\n","# Apply the categorization function\n","df_art8['article_citation_type'] = df_art8['article_numbers'].apply(categorize_article_citations)\n","\n","# Get the counts for each category\n","citation_distribution = df_art8['article_citation_type'].value_counts()\n","\n","print('Distribution of Article 8 Citation Types:')\n","display(citation_distribution.to_frame())\n","\n","# Plot the distribution\n","plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n","sns.barplot(\n","    x=citation_distribution.index,\n","    y=citation_distribution.values,\n","    hue=citation_distribution.index,\n","    palette=['#1f77b4', '#ff7f0e'],\n","    legend=False\n",")\n","plt.title('Comparison of Article 8 Citations', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Citation Type', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Cases', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"NSc-PPwRyPXR"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","The chart reveals that the majority of cases in the dataset (894 cases) cite Article 8 alongside other Convention articles, while 427 cases cite Article 8 alone. Cases involving only Article 8 are more likely to be non-violation cases, accounting for 353 out of 427 single-article cases. Where a complaint is confined to Article 8 alone, it often reflects a more contained rights issue where the Court finds the state's interference to be proportionate and justified.\n","\n","By contrast, mixed-article cases typically involve more severe human rights situations and correspondingly account for the majority of violation findings in the dataset. This distribution suggests that citation type may itself be a useful signal in the dataset, though it should not be taken as a direct prediction for outcome, as mixed cases also contain non-violations.\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"l-rJ9MVuulnt"},"source":["#####4.3.1 Article Pairing per year"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Yyy94HOmuSOC","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":416},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790642677,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":268,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"7f05b8ef-8f83-4006-8093-84aefefab705"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Group by year and article_citation_type to count cases\n","cases_by_citation_type_per_year = df_art8.groupby(['year', 'article_citation_type']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n","\n","# Ensure only 'Article 8 Only' and 'Mixed Articles' are considered for plotting\n","cases_by_citation_type_per_year = cases_by_citation_type_per_year[['Article 8 Only', 'Mixed Articles']]\n","\n","# Sort by year to ensure correct plotting order\n","cases_by_citation_type_per_year = cases_by_citation_type_per_year.sort_index()\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n","sns.lineplot(data=cases_by_citation_type_per_year, marker='o', dashes=False)\n","\n","plt.title('Trend of Article 8 Citation Types Per Year (2010-2023)', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Cases', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='Article Citation Type', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ZUu2dbTW1d4m"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","Notably, 2022 saw a spike in both mixed-article citations and violation findings, which coincides with Russia becoming the top respondent state that year. This is likely attributable to the Council of Europe's expulsion of Russia in March 2022 following the invasion of Ukraine, after which a significant volume of pending Russian cases were processed and decided.\n","\n","Given that many of these cases concerned serious and multifaceted rights violations, the surge in mixed-article cases and violation outcomes in 2022 is consistent with this geopolitical context."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"wy0vQ4pU5Qe3"},"source":["Mixed Articles cases consistently outnumber Article 8 Only cases — throughout 2010-2023, cases citing Article 8 alongside other articles outnumber standalone Article 8 cases, typically by a ratio of roughly 2:1 to 3:1. However, Article 8 Only cases have grown substantially since 2016, suggesting an increasing focus on pure privacy and family life complaints."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"4SxlD9WnFIYO"},"source":["####4.3.2 Top Article Pairing"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"85559665","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790642763,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":78,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"39a77950-d0fc-4ae8-e059-ff0ac941381c"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Processed 894 'Mixed Articles' cases.\n","Found 894 article sets.\n","Top 10 most frequent article sets:\n","  Articles (8, 41): 91 times\n","  Articles (8, 35, 41): 76 times\n","  Articles (8, 13): 57 times\n","  Articles (6, 8): 44 times\n","  Articles (3, 8): 40 times\n","  Articles (8, 35): 39 times\n","  Articles (3, 8, 13): 34 times\n","  Articles (3, 5, 8, 13): 25 times\n","  Articles (8, 14): 21 times\n","  Articles (6, 8, 35, 41): 21 times\n"]}],"source":["import re\n","from collections import Counter\n","\n","# 1. Filter the df_art8 DataFrame to include only cases where the 'article_citation_type' is 'Mixed Articles'.\n","df_mixed_articles = df_art8[df_art8['article_citation_type'] == 'Mixed Articles'].copy()\n","\n","# 2. Initialize an empty list named all_article_sets.\n","all_article_sets = []\n","\n","# 3. Iterate through the 'article_numbers' column of the df_mixed_articles DataFrame.\n","for articles_list in df_mixed_articles['article_numbers']:\n","    if isinstance(articles_list, list) and articles_list:\n","        # 4. Clean the data: convert to string, strip, convert numeric strings to integers.\n","        cleaned_articles = []\n","        for item in articles_list:\n","            s_item = str(item).strip()\n","            if s_item.isdigit():\n","                cleaned_articles.append(int(s_item))\n","\n","        # Ensure the resulting list of cleaned articles is not empty\n","        if cleaned_articles:\n","            # 5. Extract unique article numbers, sort them, and convert to a tuple.\n","            unique_sorted_articles = tuple(sorted(list(set(cleaned_articles))))\n","            all_article_sets.append(unique_sorted_articles)\n","\n","# 6. Use the Counter class from the collections module to count the frequency of each unique article set.\n","set_counts = Counter(all_article_sets)\n","\n","print(f\"Processed {len(df_mixed_articles)} 'Mixed Articles' cases.\")\n","print(f\"Found {len(all_article_sets)} article sets.\")\n","print(\"Top 10 most frequent article sets:\")\n","for article_set, count in set_counts.most_common(10):\n","    print(f\"  Articles {article_set}: {count} times\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"9-fVnpQUhHrV"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","Article 41 dominates the article combinations, appearing in the top two pairings, 8+41 (91 cases) and 8+35+41 (76 cases). This is expected since Article 41 (just satisfaction) is always cited alongside any substantive violation finding to award compensation, and is consistent with the outcome-consequent language identified in the pecuniary damage concordance analysis.\n","\n","Article 35 (admissibility) appears frequently in combinations such as (8+35+ 41) and (8+35), suggesting that a substantial number of cases involved admissibility challenges before reaching the merits determination.\n","\n","Article 13 (right to an effective remedy) is the most meaningful companion article, appearing in 8+13 (57 cases) and 3+8+13 (34 cases). This reflects a recurring pattern where applicants argue both a substantive Article 8 violation and the failure of domestic remedies.\n","\n","\n","Article 3 (prohibition of torture and inhuman treatment) pairs frequently with Article 8, appearing in (3+8), (3+8+13) and (3+5+8+13). This reflects cases involving surveillance, detention conditions or family separation where both dignity and privacy rights are at stake.\n","\n","Article 6 (right to a fair trial) also pairs notably with Article 8, appearing in 6+8 (44 cases) and 6+8+35+41 (21 cases), reflecting cases where procedural fairness complaints accompanied the Article 8 merits. Article 14 (prohibition of discrimination) appears in 8+14 (21 cases), pointing to cases where Article 8 rights were engaged alongside discrimination complaints, a recognised pairing in cases concerning minority and LGBTQ+ rights."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"097d51e0","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":938},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790642929,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":171,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"d5b2b000-f4e8-4ee2-efe2-5b49a68d55b5"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Top 10 Most Frequent Article Sets in 'Mixed Articl