": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 52,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 111,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 5,\n        \"samples\": [\n          101,\n          107,\n          64\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": 4,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 43,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 167,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 10,\n        \"samples\": [\n          56,\n          72,\n          47\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# 1. Identify the top 10 originating bodies (courts) by case count\n","top_10_courts = df_art8['court'].value_counts().nlargest(10).index.tolist()\n","\n","# 2. Filter df_art8 to include only these top 10 courts\n","df_top_courts_importance = df_art8[df_art8['court'].isin(top_10_courts)].copy()\n","\n","# 3. Calculate average importance per court (used for ordering only)\n","average_importance_per_court = df_top_courts_importance.groupby('court')['importance'].mean().sort_values(ascending=False)\n","\n","# 4. Importance distribution per court\n","importance_distribution_per_court = df_top_courts_importance.groupby(['court', 'importance']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n","importance_distribution_per_court = importance_distribution_per_court.loc[average_importance_per_court.index]\n","\n","print('\\nDistribution of Importance Levels per Originating Body:')\n","display(importance_distribution_per_court)\n","\n","custom_importance_palette = ['#414487', '#2a788e', '#22a884', '#7ad151']\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n","importance_distribution_per_court.plot(kind='bar', stacked=True, color=custom_importance_palette, ax=plt.gca())\n","plt.title('Distribution of Importance Levels by Originating Body', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Originating Body (Court)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Cases', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='Importance Level', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"sTg7wDTA55Li"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","Court type is a strong proxy for case importance. Committee formations, Fourth Section Committee, Fifth Section Committee, Third Section Committee, and Second Section Committee, handle almost exclusively importance level 4 cases, reflecting their role in processing straightforward or repetitive cases. Chamber sections (First through Fifth) handle mostly level 3 cases with a smaller proportion of level 2 and level 1 cases. The Grand Chamber, by contrast, handles almost exclusively level 1 cases, consistent with its role in deciding cases of the highest legal significance.\n","\n","This structural relationship means that court and importance level are highly correlated variables in the dataset. In the modelling stage, including both as independent features in a classification model without careful consideration would introduce multicollinearity, potentially distorting feature importance estimates.\n","\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"GogXFFLXMwkp"},"source":["####4.4.3 Importance over Time"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"EzN2AI9FQx3q","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":416},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790644245,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":346,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"57e8d15d-1432-403c-ac96-fe5e0f3bd0cc"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# 1. Group df_art8 by 'year' and 'importance' and count occurrences\n","importance_over_time = df_art8.groupby(['year', 'importance']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n","\n","# 2. Line chart of importance levels over time\n","custom_importance_palette = ['#414487', '#2a788e', '#22a884', '#7ad151']\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\n","sns.lineplot(\n","    data=importance_over_time,\n","    marker='o',\n","    dashes=False,\n","    palette=custom_importance_palette\n",")\n","plt.title('Distribution of Case Importance Levels Over Time (2010-2023)', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Cases', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='Importance Level', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"rLvA1X2IhLon"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","The distribution of importance levels over time shows that level 3 cases consistently dominate the dataset throughout the period, with level 4 cases rising steadily from 2017 onwards. Both levels peak sharply in 2022 before declining in 2023, consistent with the surge and subsequent resolution of Russian cases identified earlier. Notably, importance level 2 cases effectively disappear after 2017, while level 1 cases, the most legally significant, remain low and stable throughout before declining to near zero by 2023. The near-absence of level 1 cases in recent years may reflect the Grand Chamber's reduced caseload as the Court prioritised processing the accumulated backlog of routine cases."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"fcU3tL_MM1u9"},"source":["####4.4.4 Importance vs Section Length"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"dbc1b884","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790644300,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":51,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"7141f44c-098f-4e3a-d58a-3135e8216e49"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Helper functions extract_content_recursive, get_facts_text, and get_law_text defined.\n"]}],"source":["# Helper function to recursively extract all content from nested dictionaries\n","def extract_content_recursive(data):\n","    text_parts = []\n","    if isinstance(data, dict):\n","        if 'content' in data and isinstance(data['content'], str):\n","            text_parts.append(data['content'])\n","        if 'elements' in data and isinstance(data['elements'], list):\n","            for element in data['elements']:\n","                text_parts.extend(extract_content_recursive(element))\n","    return text_parts\n","\n","# Function to extract only the 'facts' section text from a case's full_text dictionary\n","def get_facts_text(full_text_data):\n","    if not isinstance(full_text_data, dict) or not full_text_data:\n","        return ''\n","    # Assuming the structure is {'doc_id': [list_of_sections]}\n","    sections_list = list(full_text_data.values())[0]\n","    for section_dict in sections_list:\n","        if isinstance(section_dict, dict) and section_dict.get('section_name') == 'facts':\n","            return ' '.join(extract_content_recursive(section_dict))\n","    return ''\n","\n","# Function to extract only the 'law' section text from a case's full_text dictionary\n","def get_law_text(full_text_data):\n","    if not isinstance(full_text_data, dict) or not full_text_data:\n","        return ''\n","    # Assuming the structure is {'doc_id': [list_of_sections]}\n","    sections_list = list(full_text_data.values())[0]\n","    for section_dict in sections_list:\n","        if isinstance(section_dict, dict) and section_dict.get('section_name') == 'law':\n","            return ' '.join(extract_content_recursive(section_dict))\n","    return ''\n","\n","print('Helper functions extract_content_recursive, get_facts_text, and get_law_text defined.')"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"3148e077","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":441},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790645252,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":956,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"b0b1043d-693f-4f9d-9e29-2c74e7b42f37"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x600 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Average Length per Importance Level:\n","              law_length  facts_length\n","importance                            \n","1           66926.264706  45113.617647\n","2           49635.380000  48604.560000\n","3           38078.119835  32337.274793\n","4           17730.505109  13202.572263\n"]}],"source":["# Create a new DataFrame for this analysis, selecting relevant columns from df_art8\n","df_importance_lengths = df_art8[['itemid', 'importance', 'full_text']].copy()\n","\n","# Extract facts and law sections using the helper functions\n","# Assuming get_facts_text and get_law_text are already defined from previous cells (8ec5cc3f and Fch9-tfzCLvI)\n","df_importance_lengths['facts_section'] = df_importance_lengths['full_text'].apply(get_facts_text)\n","df_importance_lengths['law_section'] = df_importance_lengths['full_text'].apply(get_law_text)\n","\n","# 1. Calculate Lengths (Character counts)\n","df_importance_lengths['facts_length'] = df_importance_lengths['facts_section'].str.len()\n","df_importance_lengths['law_length'] = df_importance_lengths['law_section'].str.len()\n","\n","# Filter out rows where facts_length or law_length are NaN (i.e., section was empty or not found)\n","df_importance_lengths = df_importance_lengths.dropna(subset=['facts_length', 'law_length'])\n","\n","# Ensure lengths are integers\n","df_importance_lengths['facts_length'] = df_importance_lengths['facts_length'].astype(int)\n","df_importance_lengths['law_length'] = df_importance_lengths['law_length'].astype(int)\n","\n","# --- FIX: Ensure 'importance' is clean and then converted to string before categorical ---\n","# Convert importance to numeric (handling potential non-numeric entries) and drop any NaNs\n","df_importance_lengths['importance'] = pd.to_numeric(df_importance_lengths['importance'], errors='coerce')\n","df_importance_lengths.dropna(subset=['importance'], inplace=True)\n","# Convert to integer and then to string to match the categorical labels\n","df_importance_lengths['importance'] = df_importance_lengths['importance'].astype(int).astype(str)\n","\n","# 2. Convert Importance to an ordered Category\n","df_importance_lengths['importance'] = pd.Categorical(df_importance_lengths['importance'],\n","                                              categories=['1', '2', '3', '4'],\n","                                              ordered=True)\n","\n","# 3. Visualize using Boxplots\n","plt.figure(figsize=(14, 6))\n","\n","# Subplot 1: Law Section Length\n","plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n","sns.boxplot(x='importance', y='law_length', data=df_importance_lengths)\n","plt.title('Correlation: Importance vs. Law Section Length')\n","plt.xlabel('Importance Level')\n","plt.ylabel('Length (Characters)')\n","\n","# Subplot 2: Facts Section Length\n","plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n","sns.boxplot(x='importance', y='facts_length', data=df_importance_lengths)\n","plt.title('Correlation: Importance vs. Facts Section Length')\n","plt.xlabel('Importance Level')\n","plt.ylabel('Length (Characters)')\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","# 4. Show the Statistical \"Truth\"\n","summary = df_importance_lengths.groupby('importance', observed=True)[['law_length', 'facts_length']].mean()\n","print(\"Average Length per Importance Level:\")\n","print(summary)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ErxApkx4G2AE"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","**The \"Law\" Section is the True Signal**\n","\n","The Law Section (The Court's Assessment) shows the most dramatic correlation. In a Level 1 case, the Court isn't just deciding a violation; it is writing a \"mini-treatise\" on Article 8.\n","\n","\n","**The \"Facts\" Section \"Saturates\"**\n","\n","While Level 1 facts are longer, the gap between Level 1 and Level 2 facts is often smaller than the gap in their Law sections.\n","\n","**Analysis:**\n","- A case might have incredibly complex facts (Level 2) but only involve a routine application of law. Conversely, a simple fact pattern (Level 1) might trigger a massive legal debate if it's the first time the ECHR is seeing a specific technology (like AI-driven surveillance).\n","- Many Level 4 cases (Importance 4) are actually very short because they refer back to \"well-established case-law\" (WECL).\n","**Risk:** If you include too many Level 4 cases in your Model, the AI might learn to predict \"No Violation\" based simply on the brevity of the text rather than the content of the law."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"JJHTieqhuwve"},"source":["\n","\n","---\n","\n","\n","#**5. Visualizations**"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ot1cP_8BEAkJ"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","For the visualizations we will focus on the Facts and Law sections of the judgments as they represent the substantive core of every ECtHR judgment. The Facts section narrates the circumstances that gave rise to the alleged violation, while the Law section contains the Court's doctrinal reasoning, including its proportionality analysis and application of Article 8-specific principles such as the margin of appreciation. Together, they capture the Court's full consideration before reaching a verdict, making them the most meaningful textual input for a classification model.\n","\n","The remaining sections were excluded on the grounds that they are largely formulaic and structural, and therefore unlikely to be informative for classification. The Procedure section contains administrative details such as dates, representative identities, and Chamber composition. The Relevant Domestic Law subsection repeats the same domestic statutes across cases from the same respondent state."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"562db7d2","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790654567,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":9318,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"c8fda0f6-c9f8-4c48-81af-2dddb17019fc"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["'parsed_full_text' column created for 1321 cases.\n","Filtered cases for 'Violation' or 'No Violation': 1265\n","TfidfVectorizer initialized with stop_words='english', min_df=0.01, max_df=0.9.\n","TF-IDF matrix created with shape: (1265, 10101)\n"]}],"source":["import json\n","from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n","\n","# Helper function to recursively extract all content\n","def extract_content_recursive(data):\n","    text_parts = []\n","    if isinstance(data, dict):\n","        if 'content' in data and isinstance(data['content'], str):\n","            text_parts.append(data['content'])\n","        if 'elements' in data and isinstance(data['elements'], list):\n","            for element in data['elements']:\n","                text_parts.extend(extract_content_recursive(element))\n","    return text_parts\n","\n","# 1. Apply the extract_content_recursive function to create parsed_full_text\n","def parse_full_text(full_text_data):\n","    if isinstance(full_text_data, dict):\n","        # Assuming the structure is {'doc_id': [list_of_sections]}\n","        for doc_id, sections_list in full_text_data.items():\n","            # Concatenate content from all sections within the document\n","            all_content = []\n","            for section_dict in sections_list:\n","                all_content.extend(extract_content_recursive(section_dict))\n","            return ' '.join(all_content)\n","    return '' # Return empty string for unparseable or empty entries\n","\n","df_art8['parsed_full_text'] = df_art8['full_text'].apply(parse_full_text)\n","print(f\"'parsed_full_text' column created for {len(df_art8)} cases.\")\n","\n","# 2. Filter df_art8 to create df_filtered_cases\n","df_filtered_cases = df_art8[\n","    (df_art8['outcome_category'] == 'Violation') |\n","    (df_art8['outcome_category'] == 'No Violation')\n","].copy()\n","print(f\"Filtered cases for 'Violation' or 'No Violation': {len(df_filtered_cases)}\")\n","\n","# 3. Import TfidfVectorizer (already done at the top of the cell)\n","\n","# 4. Initialize a TfidfVectorizer\n","tfidf_vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(stop_words='english', min_df=0.01, max_df=0.9)\n","print(\"TfidfVectorizer initialized with stop_words='english', min_df=0.01, max_df=0.9.\")\n","\n","# 5. Fit and transform the parsed_full_text column\n","tfidf_matrix = tfidf_vectorizer.fit_transform(df_filtered_cases['parsed_full_text'])\n","\n","print(f\"TF-IDF matrix created with shape: {tfidf_matrix.shape}\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"qo6aOd6N3xgY"},"source":["##5.1 N-Gram"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"wBNbnDWVCuWs"},"source":["###5.1.1 Overview (Full Case)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"aXBFehWiJ42q"},"source":["Most Frequent N-gram"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"782283b1","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790663067,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":8493,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"41d6c24b-1344-45f5-f795-a08902428a52"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["'parsed_full_text' column created for 1321 cases.\n","Filtered cases for 'Violation' or 'No Violation': 154\n","Filtered cases with non-empty 'parsed_full_text': 154\n","'parsed_facts_text' and 'parsed_law_text' columns created for df_filtered_cases.\n","CountVectorizer initialized for full text with ngram_range=(1,3), stop_words='english', min_df=5, max_df=0.55.\n","Vocabulary built for full text with 21998 n-grams.\n","DataFrame of n-gram trends for full text created (df_ngram_trends).\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer # Changed from TfidfVectorizer\n","import re # Ensure re is imported for extract_content_recursive\n","\n","# Helper function to recursively extract all content (copied from pU7bzADBiZaK to ensure availability)\n","def extract_content_recursive(data):\n","    text_parts = []\n","    if isinstance(data, dict):\n","        if 'content' in data and isinstance(data['content'], str):\n","            text_parts.append(data['content'])\n","        if 'elements' in data and isinstance(data['elements'], list):\n","            for element in data['elements']:\n","                text_parts.extend(extract_content_recursive(element))\n","    return text_parts\n","\n","# Helper function to extract structured findings (copied from KcJfzyOVnEmO to ensure availability)\n","def extract_finding_structured(conclusion_list):\n","    \"\"\"Extract Article 8 finding from the structured conclusion column.\"\"\"\n","    if not isinstance(conclusion_list, list):\n","        return 'Only Mentioning'\n","\n","    for item in conclusion_list:\n","        if not isinstance(item, dict):\n","            continue\n","        # Check base_article, article, AND element text for any Art. 8 reference\n","        is_art8 = (\n","            item.get('base_article') == '8' or\n","            item.get('article') == '8' or\n","            '8' in str(item.get('details', '')) or\n","            re.search(r'art(icle)?\\.?\\s*8', str(item.get('element', '')), re.IGNORECASE)\n","        )\n","        if is_art8:\n","            if item.get('type') == 'violation':\n","                return 'Violation'\n","            elif item.get('type') == 'no-violation':\n","                return 'No Violation'\n","\n","    return 'Only Mentioning'\n","\n","# Helper function to extract only the 'facts' section text\n","def get_facts_text(full_text_data):\n","    if not isinstance(full_text_data, dict) or not full_text_data:\n","        return ''\n","    sections_list = list(full_text_data.values())[0]\n","    for section_dict in sections_list:\n","        if isinstance(section_dict, dict) and section_dict.get('section_name') == 'facts':\n","            return ' '.join(extract_content_recursive(section_dict))\n","    return ''\n","\n","# Helper function to extract only the 'law' section text\n","def get_law_text(full_text_data):\n","    if not isinstance(full_text_data, dict) or not full_text_data:\n","        return ''\n","    sections_list = list(full_text_data.values())[0]\n","    for section_dict in sections_list:\n","        if isinstance(section_dict, dict) and section_dict.get('section_name') == 'law':\n","            return ' '.join(extract_content_recursive(section_dict))\n","    return ''\n","\n","# Ensure PALETTE is available from the setup cell (copied from zEN6dfLxoyM1)\n","PALETTE = {'Violation': '#d62728', 'No Violation': '#2ca02c', 'Others': '#aec7e8'}\n","\n","# Apply the structured extraction function to create 'finding_structured' (copied from KcJfzyOVnEmO)\n","df_art8['finding_structured'] = df_raw.loc[df_art8.index, 'conclusion'].apply(extract_finding_structured)\n","\n","# Use the structured conclusion column for more accurate outcome extraction (copied from zEN6dfLxoyM1)\n","# (see comparison note above — structured approach catches combined article findings)\n","df_art8['outcome_category'] = df_art8['finding_structured'].replace('Only Mentioning', 'Others')\n","\n","# 1. Parse full text for all cases (all sections excluding boilerplate)\n","def parse_full_text(full_text_data):\n","    if isinstance(full_text_data, dict):\n","        for doc_id, sections_list in full_text_data.items():\n","            all_content = []\n","            for section_dict in sections_list:\n","                # Exclude toc and appendix boilerplate\n","                section_name = section_dict.get('section_name', '').lower()\n","                if section_name in ['toc', 'appendix']:\n","                    continue\n","                all_content.extend(extract_content_recursive(section_dict))\n","            return ' '.join(all_content)\n","    return ''\n","\n","df_art8['parsed_full_text'] = df_art8['full_text'].apply(parse_full_text)\n","print(f\"'parsed_full_text' column created for {len(df_art8)} cases.\")\n","\n","# 2. Filter to Violation and No Violation only\n","df_filtered_cases = df_art8[\n","    df_art8['outcome_category'].isin(['Violation', 'No Violation'])\n","].copy()\n","print(f\"Filtered cases for 'Violation' or 'No Violation': {len(df_filtered_cases)}\")\n","\n","# Filter out cases where full text might be empty after extraction (optional, but good for corpus quality)\n","df_full_text_filtered = df_filtered_cases[df_filtered_cases['parsed_full_text'].str.strip() != ''].copy()\n","print(f\"Filtered cases with non-empty 'parsed_full_text': {len(df_full_text_filtered)}\")\n","\n","# Apply the functions to df_filtered_cases to get 'facts' and 'law' text\n","df_filtered_cases['parsed_facts_text'] = df_filtered_cases['full_text'].apply(get_facts_text)\n","df_filtered_cases['parsed_law_text'] = df_filtered_cases['full_text'].apply(get_law_text)\n","print(f\"'parsed_facts_text' and 'parsed_law_text' columns created for df_filtered_cases.\")\n","\n","# 3. Initialize a CountVectorizer for full text\n","count_vectorizer_full_text = CountVectorizer(\n","    ngram_range=(1, 3),\n","    stop_words='english',\n","    min_df=5,\n","    max_df=0.55\n",")\n","print(\"CountVectorizer initialized for full text with ngram_range=(1,3), stop_words='english', min_df=5, max_df=0.55.\")\n","\n","# 4. Build vocabulary from all filtered full texts\n","count_vectorizer_full_text.fit(df_full_text_filtered['parsed_full_text'])\n","feature_names_full_text = count_vectorizer_full_text.get_feature_names_out()\n","print(f\"Vocabulary built for full text with {len(feature_names_full_text)} n-grams.\")\n","\n","# 5. Create an empty list to store n-gram counts per year for full text\n","ngram_trends_full_text_list = []\n","\n","# 6. Get unique years\n","unique_years_full_text = sorted(df_full_text_filtered['year'].unique())\n","\n","# 7. Iterate through each year and process n-grams\n","for year in unique_years_full_text:\n","    df_year_full_text = df_full_text_filtered[df_full_text_filtered['year'] == year]\n","    if not df_year_full_text.empty:\n","        yearly_ngram_matrix_full_text = count_vectorizer_full_text.transform(df_year_full_text['parsed_full_text'])\n","        ngram_counts_for_year_full_text = yearly_ngram_matrix_full_text.sum(axis=0)\n","        ngram_counts_dict_full_text = {name: count for name, count in zip(feature_names_full_text, ngram_counts_for_year_full_text.tolist()[0])}\n","        ngram_trends_full_text_list.append({'year': year, **ngram_counts_dict_full_text})\n","    else:\n","        ngram_trends_full_text_list.append({'year': year, **{name: 0 for name in feature_names_full_text}})\n","\n","# 8. Convert to pandas DataFrame and set 'year' as index, fill NaN with 0\n","df_ngram_trends = pd.DataFrame(ngram_trends_full_text_list).set_index('year').fillna(0)\n","df_ngram_trends = df_ngram_trends.astype(int)\n","print(\"DataFrame of n-gram trends for full text created (df_ngram_trends).\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Yp7R8CJ8mOLS","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790663113,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":41,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"ea5e02a0-30d1-41fb-8d7e-4ed111f280d7"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Class distribution in filtered cases:\n","outcome_category\n","Violation       118\n","No Violation     36\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n","Violation rate: 76.6%\n"]}],"source":["pr