n)\n","top_50_ngrams_overall = df_ngram_trends.sum().nlargest(50).index.tolist()\n","\n","# 2. Select only these top 50 n-grams from the trends DataFrame\n","df_top_50_ngrams = df_ngram_trends[top_50_ngrams_overall]\n","\n","# 3. Calculate the year-over-year percentage change\n","percentage_change = df_top_50_ngrams.pct_change() * 100\n","\n","# Handle infinite values (from 0 to non-zero change) or very large changes for better visualization\n","percentage_change = percentage_change.clip(lower=-200, upper=200).fillna(0)\n","\n","# Calculate the maximum absolute change for each n-gram across all years\n","max_abs_change = percentage_change.abs().max()\n","\n","# Identify the top 10 n-grams with the biggest absolute change\n","top_10_biggest_change_ngrams = max_abs_change.nlargest(10).index.tolist()\n","print(f\"Top 10 n-grams with biggest year-over-year change: {top_10_biggest_change_ngrams}\")\n","\n","# 4. Visualize the trends of these top 10 percentage changes\n","plt.figure(figsize=(18, 10))\n","sns.lineplot(data=percentage_change[top_10_biggest_change_ngrams])\n","plt.title('Year-over-Year Percentage Change of Top 10 N-grams with Biggest Change (Full Case Text)', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Percentage Change (%)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='N-gram', bbox_to_anchor=(1.02, 1), loc='upper left', borderaxespad=0.)\n","plt.axhline(0, color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=0.8) # Add a line at 0% for reference\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"mWcEoaGHzeSd"},"source":["**Note:**\n","\n","The year-over-year percentage change analysis identifies the ten most volatile n-grams in the dataset. All ten terms exhibit high volatility throughout the period, with frequent large swings in both directions, indicating that their frequency is sensitive to the specific composition of cases in each year rather than reflecting stable long-term trends. The terms include substantive legal concepts, \"detention\", \"surveillance\", \"search\", \"investigation\", and \"data\", alongside case-specific references such as \"russian\", \"2002\", and \"2015\", the latter likely reflecting the citation of specific precedents whose frequency fluctuates as relevant cases are decided. Most terms show a sharp decline in 2022-2023, consistent with the overall reduction in case volume following the resolution of the Russian caseload. The volatility of these terms suggests they may be unreliable as stable predictive features across time periods, a consideration relevant to temporal generalisation of any trained model."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"mkO85YUQAr_k"},"source":["###5.1.3 Facts Section"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"8ec5cc3f","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":594},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790666137,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":2395,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"45361625-c981-43e1-fc2b-d97b7de1818c"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["'parsed_facts_text' column created. First entry preview (first 200 chars):\n","\n","THE FACTS I.  THE CIRCUMSTANCES OF THE CASE 5.  The applicant was born in 1951. His daughter and son were born in 1996 and 1999 respectively. 6.  The applicant and the mother of the above-mentioned gi\n","\n","Filtered cases with non-empty 'facts' text: 145\n","CountVectorizer initialized for 'facts' section with ngram_range=(2,3), stop_words='english', min_df=5, max_df=0.55.\n","Vocabulary built for 'facts' section with 3310 n-grams.\n","DataFrame of n-gram trends for 'facts' section created.\n","Top 10 most frequent n-grams in 'facts' section: ['district court', 'second applicant', 'supreme court', 'criminal proceedings', 'court appeal', 'human rights', 'regional court', 'constitutional court', 'prose