ext: {len(df_facts_filtered)}\")\n","\n","# 1. Initialize a CountVectorizer for facts section\n","count_vectorizer_facts = CountVectorizer(\n","    ngram_range=(2, 3),\n","    stop_words='english',\n","    min_df=5,\n","    max_df=0.55\n",")\n","print(\"CountVectorizer initialized for 'facts' section with ngram_range=(2,3), stop_words='english', min_df=5, max_df=0.55.\")\n","\n","# 2. Create an empty list to store n-gram counts per year for facts\n","ngram_trends_facts_list = []\n","\n","# 3. Get unique years from df_facts_filtered\n","unique_years_facts = sorted(df_facts_filtered['year'].unique())\n","\n","# 4. Fit CountVectorizer to the entire parsed_facts_text to build a comprehensive vocabulary\n","count_vectorizer_facts.fit(df_facts_filtered['parsed_facts_text'])\n","feature_names_facts = count_vectorizer_facts.get_feature_names_out()\n","print(f\"Vocabulary built for 'facts' section with {len(feature_names_facts)} n-grams.\")\n","\n","# 5. Iterate through each year and process n-grams for facts\n","for year in unique_years_facts:\n","    # a. Filter df_facts_filtered for the current year\n","    df_year_facts = df_facts_filtered[df_facts_filtered['year'] == year]\n","\n","    # b. Transform the text for this year\n","    if not df_year_facts.empty:\n","        yearly_ngram_matrix_facts = count_vectorizer_facts.transform(df_year_facts['parsed_facts_text'])\n","        # c. Calculate the sum of counts for each n-gram within the current year\n","        ngram_counts_for_year_facts = yearly_ngram_matrix_facts.sum(axis=0)\n","        ngram_counts_dict_facts = {name: count for name, count in zip(feature_names_facts, ngram_counts_for_year_facts.tolist()[0])}\n","        # d. Append to ngram_trends_facts_list\n","        ngram_trends_facts_list.append({'year': year, **ngram_counts_dict_facts})\n","    else:\n","        # If no cases for the year, still add an entry with 0 counts for all n-grams\n","        ngram_trends_facts_list.append({'year': year, **{name: 0 for name in feature_names_facts}})\n","\n","# 6. Convert to pandas DataFrame and set 'year' as index, fill NaN with 0\n","df_ngram_trends_facts = pd.DataFrame(ngram_trends_facts_list).set_index('year').fillna(0)\n","df_ngram_trends_facts = df_ngram_trends_facts.astype(int)\n","print(\"DataFrame of n-gram trends for 'facts' section created.\")\n","\n","# 7. Calculate total frequency and identify top 10 n-grams for facts\n","top_10_ngrams_facts = df_ngram_trends_facts.sum().nlargest(10).index.tolist()\n","print(f\"Top 10 most frequent n-grams in 'facts' section: {top_10_ngrams_facts}\")\n","\n","# 8. Create a line plot for top 10 n-grams over time for facts\n","plt.figure(figsize=(16, 9))\n","sns.lineplot(data=df_ngram_trends_facts[top_10_ngrams_facts])\n","plt.title('Top N-gram Trends in \\'Facts\\' Section Over Time (2010-2023)', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('N-gram Count', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='N-gram', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Jib2X1WXfkk-"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","The top n-grams in the Facts section are dominated by references to domestic judicial institutions '**district court**', '**supreme court**', '**court appeal**', '**constitutional court**', and '**regional court**, reflecting the standard narrative structure of ECtHR judgments, which typically trace the applicant's progression through domestic courts before the case reaches Strasbourg. These terms are unlikely to carry meaningful predictive signal as they appear uniformly across both violation and non-violation cases.\n","\n","'**Criminal proceedings**' is the most substantively relevant n-gram in this section, as it identifies a specific case context in which Article 8 issues, such as covert surveillance or unlawful searches, frequently arise. 'Inter alia', like '**mutatis mutandis**' in the Law section, is a Latin structural phrase with no substantive content and should be considered for removal during preprocessing. Overall, the Facts section n-grams are predominantly procedural and institutional, reinforcing the earlier finding that the Law section is likely to yield richer predictive features for the classification task."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"00bbddc5","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790666195,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":45,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"c1e133c3-8f38-4364-f53f-9256387f7bc7"},"source":["# 1. Create a new DataFrame, df_filtered_importance\n","# Ensure 'importance' is numeric first, then filter\n","df_filtered_cases['importance'] = pd.to_numeric(df_filtered_cases['importance'], errors='coerce')\n","\n","df_filtered_importance = df_filtered_cases[\n","    (df_filtered_cases['outcome_category'].isin(['Violation', 'No Violation'])) &\n","    (df_filtered_cases['importance'].isin([1, 2]))\n","].copy()\n","\n","# Filter out cases where facts text might be empty after extraction\n","df_filtered_importance = df_filtered_importance[df_filtered_importance['parsed_facts_text'].str.strip() != ''].copy()\n","\n","print(f\"Filtered cases for Importance 1 or 2, with 'Violation' or 'No Violation' outcomes, and non-empty facts text: {len(df_filtered_importance)} cases.\")\n","\n","# 2. Initialize a CountVectorizer\n","cv_importance = CountVectorizer(\n","    ngram_range=(1, 2), # Modified to include unigrams and bigrams\n","    stop_words='english',\n","    min_df=5\n",")\n","print(\"CountVectorizer initialized for importance levels 1 & 2 facts section with ngram_range=(1, 2).\")"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Filtered cases for Importance 1 or 2, with 'Violation' or 'No Violation' outcomes, and non-empty facts text: 18 cases.\n","CountVectorizer initialized for importance levels 1 & 2 facts section with ngram_range=(1, 2).\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"-QFEAewCCIBu"},"source":["###5.1.4 Law Section"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Fch9-tfzCLvI","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":594},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790669238,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":3039,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"6555256d-3efb-43b8-fa0e-d4168009cd4b"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["'parsed_law_text' column created. First entry preview (first 200 chars):\n","\n","THE LAW I.  ALLEGED VIOLATION OF ARTICLE 8 OF THE CONVENTION 56.  The applicant complained on his own and his children’s behalf that they had been unable to enjoy family life together due to the lengt\n","\n","Filtered cases with non-empty 'law' text: 153\n","CountVectorizer initialized for 'law' section with ngram_range=(2,3), stop_words='english', min_df=5, max_df=0.55.\n","Vocabulary built for 'law' section with 9364 n-grams.\n","DataFrame of n-gram trends for 'law' section created.\n","Top 10 most frequent n-grams in 'law' section: ['private life', 'second applicant', 'domestic remedies', 'supreme court', 'human rights', 'mutatis mutandis', 'domestic authorities', 'court appeal', 'article 14', 'margin appreciation']\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1600x900 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Helper function to recursively extract all content (moved to cell 782283b1)\n","# def extract_content_recursive(data):\n","#     text_parts = []\n","#     if isinstance(data, dict):\n","#         if 'content' in data and isinstance(data['content'], str):\n","#             text_parts.append(data['content'])\n","#         if 'elements' in data and isinstance(data['elements'], list):\n","#             for element in data['elements']:\n","#                 text_parts.extend(extract_content_recursive(element))\n","#     return text_parts\n","\n","# Function to extract only the 'law' section text for a given full_text dictionary (moved to cell 782283b1)\n","# def get_law_text(full_text_data):\n","#     if not isinstance(full_text_data, dict) or not full_text_data:\n","#         return ''\n","\n","#     # Assuming the structure is {'doc_id': [list_of_sections]}\n","#     sections_list = list(full_text_data.values())[0]\n","\n","#     for section_dict in sections_list:\n","#         if isinstance(section_dict, dict) and section_dict.get('section_name') == 'law':\n","#             return ' '.join(extract_content_recursive(section_dict))\n","#     return ''\n","\n","# Apply the function to df_filtered_cases to get only 'law' text (moved to cell 782283b1)\n","# df_filtered_cases['parsed_law_text'] = df_filtered_cases['full_text'].apply(get_law_text)\n","print(f\"'parsed_law_text' column created. First entry preview (first 200 chars):\\n\")\n","print(df_filtered_cases['parsed_law_text'].iloc[0][:200])\n","\n","# Filter out cases where law text might be empty after extraction (moved from 6.2.3)\n","df_law_filtered = df_filtered_cases[df_filtered_cases['parsed_law_text'].str.strip() != ''].copy()\n","print(f\"\\nFiltered cases with non-empty 'law' text: {len(df_law_filtered)}\")\n","\n","# 1. Initialize a CountVectorizer for law section\n","count_vectorizer_law = CountVectorizer(\n","    ngram_range=(2, 3),\n","    stop_words='english',\n","    min_df=5,\n","    max_df=0.55\n",")\n","print(\"CountVectorizer initialized for 'law' section with ngram_range=(2,3), stop_words='english', min_df=5, max_df=0.55.\")\n","\n","# 2. Create an empty list to store n-gram counts per year for law\n","ngram_trends_law_list = []\n","\n","# 3. Get unique years from df_law_filtered\n","unique_years_law = sorted(df_law_filtered['year'].unique())\n","\n","# 4. Fit CountVectorizer to the entire parsed_law_text to build a comprehensive vocabulary\n","count_vectorizer_law.fit(df_law_filtered['parsed_law_text'])\n","feature_names_law = count_vectorizer_law.get_feature_names_out()\n","print(f\"Vocabulary built for 'law' section with {len(feature_names_law)} n-grams.\")\n","\n","# 5. Iterate through each year and process n-grams for law\n","for year in unique_years_law:\n","    # a. Filter df_law_filtered for the current year\n","    df_year_law = df_law_filtered[df_law_filtered['year'] == year]\n","\n","    # b. Transform the text for this year\n","    if not df_year_law.empty:\n","        yearly_ngram_matrix_law = count_vectorizer_law.transform(df_year_law['parsed_law_text'])\n","        # c. Calculate the sum of counts for each n-gram within the current year\n","        ngram_counts_for_year_law = yearly_ngram_matrix_law.sum(axis=0)\n","        ngram_counts_dict_law = {name: count for name, count in zip(feature_names_law, ngram_counts_for_year_law.tolist()[0])}\n","        # d. Append to ngram_trends_law_list\n","        ngram_trends_law_list.append({'year': year, **ngram_counts_dict_law})\n","    else:\n","        # If no cases for the year, still add an entry with 0 counts for all n-grams\n","        ngram_trends_law_list.append({'year': year, **{name: 0 for name in feature_names_law}})\n","\n","# 6. Convert to pandas DataFrame and set 'year' as index, fill NaN with 0\n","df_ngram_trends_law = pd.DataFrame(ngram_trends_law_list).set_index('year').fillna(0)\n","df_ngram_trends_law = df_ngram_trends_law.astype(int)\n","print(\"DataFrame of n-gram trends for 'law' section created.\")\n","\n","# 7. Calculate total frequency and identify top 10 n-grams for law\n","top_10_ngrams_law = df_ngram_trends_law.sum().nlargest(10).index.tolist()\n","print(f\"Top 10 most frequent n-grams in 'law' section: {top_10_ngrams_law}\")\n","\n","# 8. Create a line plot for top 10 n-grams over time for law\n","plt.figure(figsize=(16, 9))\n","sns.lineplot(data=df_ngram_trends_law[top_10_ngrams_law])\n","plt.title('Top N-gram Trends in \\'Law\\' Section Over Time (2010-2023)', fontsize=16)\n","plt.xlabel('Year', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('N-gram Count', fontsize=12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n","plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n","plt.legend(title='N-gram', bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 1), loc='upper left')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"e-w_wq4_5U0l"},"source":["**Note :**\n","\n","Within the Law section, several n-grams appears to have legal significance.\n","- **'Margin of appreciation'** is particularly notable, as it reflects the Court's doctrine of deference to member states, which may correlate with non-violation findings where the Court concludes the state acted within permissible discretion.\n","- **'Respect for private life'** is the core of Article 8(1).\n","- **'Best interests'** mainly appears in child-related cases such as custody or immigration, where failure to properly balanced the child's interest often results in a violation finding.\n","- **'Article 13'(right to an effective remedy)** could also be indicative of violation finding. Based on the n-grams, the law section is more informative than the Facts section, which suggests that feature extraction from this section may be more beneficial for the classication model.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"vma8lDwk3oXq"},"source":["##5.2 ScatterText"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"7be352d9","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1775790705359,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":36101,"user":{"displayName":"Rini P","userId":"15518706882043159565"}},"outputId":"34c9bbee-cb33-40b2-bace-a4d622b319ea"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Collecting scattertext\n","  Downloading scattertext-0.2.2-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (581 bytes)\n","Requirement already satisfied: numpy>=1.2.6 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from scattertext) (2.0.2)\n","Collecting scipy<1.1